==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|kibbitzer}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|kibitz|er|id2=agent noun}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who offers unsolicited views, advice, or criticism; one who [[kibitz]]es.
#: {{ux|en|Did I ask you what you thought about my cards, you '''kibitzer'''?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1956|month=January|work=Galaxy|title=The Gravity Business|author=w:James E. Gunn|url=https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/49897/pg49897-images.html|passage="Don't be a '''kibitzer'''!" Grampa snapped. "When I need help, I'll ask for it. No dad-blamed machine is gonna outthink Grampa!" He snorted indignantly.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=w:Anatole Broyard|title=Updike Goes All Out at Last|section=Books of The Times|work=The New York Times|date=1971-11-05|url=https://www.nytimes.com/1971/11/05/archives/updike-goes-all-out-at-last.html|issn=0362-4331|passage=Neither good nor evil exactly, he is the ultimate catalyst or '''kibitzer''', a blue-note howl of pain and laughter such as Charlie Parker might have blown.}}

